  "internal_policy": {
    "EDR_483": "Shadow hand/effect payload destroys one ordinary maximum crystal via ChangeManaCrystals(-1), then installs first persistent stage independently of physical source. First real recipient turn_started removes stage1 and installs stage2; second removes stage2 and gains two filled ordinary crystals via ChangeManaCrystals(2,filled=True), capped by original resource rules. No Objective flag, timed public-area slot or custom counter. Gain is unconditional even if destruction at zero removed nothing. Full-crystal interpretation follows wording without empty, and exact two-owner-start window remain uncalibrated internal policies.",
    "END_011": "Holy dual-class root. Real objective duration3, tick_event=turn_started; own-start trigger grants GainTemporaryMana(1) after ordinary mana refresh, before native countdown and turn draw. Three future real owner starts each reward once including last before expiry. Owner end/opponent start do not tick; temporary amount never changes max_mana or mana_cap and expires through native turn departure. Internal timing policy, not CN calibration.",
    "TIME_700": "Holy root. Real objective duration3, tick_event=turn_ended with EndTurnSpec(controller). Three real owner ends, including current ordinary owner end if installed before boundary, each request one exact TIME_700t122736 before native countdown; third reward precedes expiry, no on_expire extra reward. Counterpart end does not tick. Exact 3/5 Dragon Taunt dependency linked by both official childIds, source-independent ordinary summon attribution/quantity/capacity. Native end-body repetitions and countdown remain independent; no invented timer.",
    "boundaries": "Public full en-US/zh-CN faces confirm identity, text, child and fixed three-turn raw tags. Official gallery drops @ display placeholder; comparison removes only that known placeholder. Faces do not establish exact server trigger ordering, ramp fill policy or timer semantics. Formal standard pool and CN timing calibration incomplete."
  },
